text:
alex.kim: Quick Q — provisioning GPU node pools for the new inference cluster. We need a Terraform pattern that supports: Dedicated customers (SLA) with capacity reservations, dev/test on spot, and an automatic fallback to on-demand when spot gets reclaimed. Also any tips for k8s taints/labels and secrets/KMS access for nodes?

maria.g: For SLA workloads I'd keep a separate reserved-capacity ASG (or nodegroup) per AZ and a separate spot/mixed pool for scale-out. Reserved = capacity reservation + on-demand instances pinned. Spot pool = mixed_instances_policy with on-demand fallback. Keep them as distinct nodegroups so scheduling/taints are simple. :thumbsup:

jin.park: Terraform sketch (very condensed) — two ASGs: reserved + spot. Use launch template for reserved with capacity_reservation_spec; spot pool uses mixed_instances_policy. Example:
```hcl
resource "aws_launch_template" "reserved_lt" {
  name_prefix = "gpu-reserved-"
  instance_type = "g5.12xlarge"
  // capacity reservation binding
  capacity_reservation_spec {
    capacity_reservation_preference = "open"
  }
}
resource "aws_autoscaling_group" "reserved" {
  launch_template { id = aws_launch_template.reserved_lt.id }
  min_size = 2
  max_size = 10
  tags = [{ key = "k8s.io/cluster-autoscaler/enabled", value = "false", propagate_at_launch = true }]
}
resource "aws_autoscaling_group" "spot" {
  mixed_instances_policy { /* use spot + on-demand fallback */ }
  min_size = 0
  max_size = 50
}
```

sam_ops: A few ops notes: 1) Node IAM role needs kms:Decrypt and s3:GetObject for model blobs + ebs permissions. 2) Taint the reserved pool (e.g., gpu=reserved:NoSchedule) and label nodes with workload=dedicated so schedulers place customer pods there. 3) Cluster Autoscaler flag: use --balance-similar-node-groups and tag ASGs with k8s.io/cluster-autoscaler/<cluster-name> to allow scale-down/scale-up work.

maria.g: For fallback behavior: set spot pool mixed policy to allow on-demand instances after interruptions, but keep a small baseline of reserved nodes for SLA. Also add a PriorityClass or podAffinity rules so critical inference pods prefer reserved pool.

alex.kim: That helps. Any suggestions for capacity reservations across AZs (spread vs single AZ)? We want zone-resilience for Dedicated customers.

jin.park: Reserve per-AZ is best — create one capacity reservation per AZ and pin the reserved ASG to those AZs. Also export the reservation IDs into the launch template via capacity_reservation_spec to ensure ASG uses them. If using Terraform modules, make reservation IDs outputs so the nodegroup module can reference them.

sam_ops: Secrets wiring: use instance profile + IAM role with KMS decrypt permission OR use IRSA (recommended) so pods assume a role with KMS access. For Dedicated customers with stronger controls, prefer IRSA and IRSA-bound service account so you can revoke access without touching nodes.

alex.kim: Nice — will put up a PR with two nodegroups + taints/labels + IRSA support. Plan to default dev env to spot-only. I'll include a small plan-check in CI to ensure capacity reservation IDs are present for Dedicated deploys. :eyes:

devops-bot: terraform plan for branch alex/gpu-nodepool-provision completed — 2 changes to reserved, 1 to spot. CI passed.

maria.g: SGTM. Please add unit test for nodegroup module to catch missing reservation_id. Then tag me for review. :thumbsup:

